WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
One more view. This time from the door, where Silvector stands.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:16.500
Silvector sees an agent arrive and name the person who sent it. It greets the agent and starts a record.

3
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:27.500
It reads the signals. Our assessment: the band is moderate. A band, not a score.

4
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:38.500
It checks the delegation. The cart is allowed. Payment waits for the person.

5
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:50.500
Busy hours are rate-limited. A full cart waits for the person to confirm. Quiet hours are permitted.

6
00:00:50.500 --> 00:01:00.500
Every step is written down as a signed receipt. A neutral record of what the agent did, not another protocol.

7
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:09.500
One visit is a story. A day of simulated demo visits is a pattern: let through, asked to verify, blocked.

8
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.500
What we noticed. What we decided. And why.

10
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.500
Silvector. Seen, decided, signed.
